t-s-murder/a-78814305?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Yorgen Fenech was suspected to have masterminded the murder of investigative journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia, whose family continue to demand justice for her killing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin's punitive measures unlikely to deter Putin: experts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ee1e149cdd9e48dff093d9e83a6195035d5f3a6cfdc6edfc1c6709b17f6d490</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-punitive-measures-unlikely-to-deter-putin-experts/a-78803217--1019fd9fdcc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-punitive-measures-unlikely-to-deter-putin-experts/a-78803217?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has announced punitive measures after publicly blaming Russia for an attempted airport drone attack. But a former diplomat, political and security analysts warn it will likely do little to deter the Kremlin.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Unity at last: Is Libya's damaging power struggle at an end?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78a2997c98d8dc38ce40518374550976384ef54c6be5132823be21b6fa67232c</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/unity-at-last-is-libya-s-damaging-power-struggle-at-an-end/a-78758325--c023aa2cebed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/unity-at-last-is-libya-s-damaging-power-struggle-at-an-end/a-78758325?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For over a decade, Libya has been split between two opposing governments. Elections, meant to end the rivalry and unite the country, are now scheduled within two years.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: How to woo voters with an immigrant background</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:590e3f77856846c20cd9e6ae793ffd42d5344df3e2633efdd76ee53ef422cc0a</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-how-to-woo-voters-with-an-immigrant-background/a-78790775--d51a382b1b9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-how-to-woo-voters-with-an-immigrant-background/a-78790775?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The number of voters in Germany with an immigrant background is rising. Yet the established parties barely manage to reach them. Why not?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Macron visits Bayeux Tapestry with King Charles, PM Andy Burnham</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dded7d9b07a6d71527a9621de0beb204f05f569f3989361343ac15a98169081c</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317--2b18eacc4fb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is on a shorter-term visit to the UK than the renowned on-loan 11th century tapestry. He viewed the ancient artwork with the UK monarch and relatively new Prime Minister Andy Burnham.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's hybrid attacks on Germany: When is it 'war?'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83f3e46b42c467362b18a8c35eaa94b4448686e6b161922532a7aa70e0258409</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-hybrid-attacks-on-germany-when-is-it-war/a-78784262--fedfa401971d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-hybrid-attacks-on-germany-when-is-it-war/a-78784262?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German government is holding Russia responsible for an unsuccessful attack in Leipzig. Yet many feel that its response has been too mild.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Austria women ice hockey team fight for future generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:441733cd8573b29615b98e91cf737a1d62f752c3ba3e6005102833e901ceabfc</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578--54a1e0f96b9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Austria are getting ready for their first Women's Ice Hockey World Championship. But preparations have been overshadowed by a dispute about conditions, pay and getting men's cast-off kit. A solution now looks in sight.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>US sanctions halt TOEFL and GRE tests in Iran, disrupting study plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a52e98238978f0424c8486b9474860a9e141aed531d9f15ff3603ec502ac2e4</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T14:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-halt-toefl-and-gre-tests-in-iran-disrupting-study-plans/a-78764639--eb09c13fa9f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-halt-toefl-and-gre-tests-in-iran-disrupting-study-plans/a-78764639?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students in Iran can no longer take TOEFL and GRE exams after a US sanctions exemption was suspended. Applicants say the move threatens university deadlines and adds costly travel obligations.</summary><catego